Run the native ARM64 SteamCMD bootstrap as the steamcmd user so it can
update itself and download dedicated servers into its writable directory:

runuser -u steamcmd -- /opt/steamcmd/steamcmd.sh +quit

Check the architecture of each dedicated server separately. SteamCMD
can download server files regardless of whether their executables run
natively on ARM64.

For each server instance managed by OpenRC, symlink /etc/init.d/steamcmd
to /etc/init.d/steamcmd.<instance> and copy /etc/conf.d/steamcmd to
/etc/conf.d/steamcmd.<instance>. Configure the server executable, path
and arguments in the instance's conf.d file.

https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/SteamCMD
